g at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $733 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $313 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["GXO Logistics, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.2B market cap on $13.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $110M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 13.56\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 67% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6667097054249579},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"GXO Logistics, Inc. $GXO Stock Acquired by Pekin Hardy Strauss Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/gxo-logistics-inc-gxo-stock-acquired-by-pekin-hardy-strauss-inc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965393.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.93,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Is GXO Logistics (GXO) Reasonable After Record Contract Wins?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nyse-gxo/gxo-logistics/news/is-gxo-logistics-gxo-reasonable-after-record-contract-wins","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965012.578,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.727,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"GXO Logistics (GXO) \u2013 Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Changes","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/gxo-logistics-gxo-analysts-recent-ratings-changes.html","da